  "question": "Background / Context\nBetter Fiori is a project designed to improve the user experience for time reporting within SAP Fiori. Although SAP Fiori is a robust CRM tool, it lacks an intuitive interface for time reporting, which can be cumbersome for users. Better Fiori addresses this gap by providing a streamlined, user-friendly alternative, developed with the SQLPage framework using SQL for data management.\n\n Objectives\nThe primary objective of Better Fiori is to provide a more accessible and efficient solution for time reporting, enhancing user compliance with time tracking, and improving scheduling efficiency. The system aims to simplify time entry and submission processes for users who normally manage this through SAP Fiori.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n- Primary Users: Employees required to report working hours.\n- Administrators: Responsible for overseeing time reporting compliance and addressing any system-related issues.\n- Developers: Involved in maintaining and updating the Better Fiori application.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n1. Simplified Time Reporting: Better Fiori offers a user-centric interface, enhancing the ease and speed of entering and submitting working hours.\n2. Automated Daily Notifications: The system includes alerts reminding users to report their hours if missed on the previous day, ensuring adherence to reporting policies.\n3. Data Management with SQLPage: Utilizes the SQLPage framework to leverage SQL's robustness, ensuring reliable data handling and storage.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Scalability: The system should handle the concurrent reporting needs of all users efficiently.\n- Usability: Designed with user-friendly interfaces to minimize reporting time and errors.\n- Reliability: Offers consistent and dependable notification and reporting functionalities.\n- Flexibility: Easily integrates with existing SAP Fiori setups without significant disruptions.\n\n Database Schema Overview\nThe database schema supports the key functionalities of Better Fiori:\n- INSTALLATIONS: Stores installation data for various work environments.\n- LABORCODES and BILLINGCODES: Establish the coding systems necessary for labor and billing operations.\n- TICKETS and REPORTS: Manage and log time reporting activities, including details like creation dates, labor codes, and work hours.\n- SHELL: Configures user interface elements such as themes and menu items.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0158\nCREATE TABLE `installations` (\n  `installation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `installation_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`installation_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `laborcodes` (\n  `laborcode_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`laborcode_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `code` (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `billingcodes` (\n  `billingcode_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`billingcode_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `code` (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tickets` (\n  `ticket_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `installation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ticket_number` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `laborcode_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `billingcode_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `closed_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ticket_id`),\n  KEY `installation_id` (`installation_id`),\n  KEY `laborcode_id` (`laborcode_id`),\n  KEY `billingcode_id` (`billingcode_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tickets_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`installation_id`) REFERENCES `installations` (`installation_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tickets_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`laborcode_id`) REFERENCES `laborcodes` (`laborcode_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tickets_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`billingcode_id`) REFERENCES `billingcodes` (`billingcode_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reports` (\n  `report_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `ticket_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `laborcode_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `report_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `hours_worked` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `notes` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `submitted_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`report_id`),\n  KEY `ticket_id` (`ticket_id`),\n  KEY `laborcode_id` (`laborcode_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reports_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`ticket_id`) REFERENCES `tickets` (`ticket_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `reports_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`laborcode_id`) REFERENCES `laborcodes` (`laborcode_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `shell` (\n  `shell_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `theme_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `menu_label` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `menu_order` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `menu_url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `is_active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`shell_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
